  "system": {
    "finalName": "",
    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book: <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Unknown_Regions\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions\">Star Wars Saga Edition Unknown Regions</a></i> </p><p>Initially an attempt to duplicate both the lethality and simplicity of the Wookiee <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Bowcaster\" title=\"Bowcaster\">Bowcaster</a>, the Magna Caster is unable to replicate the penetration or power of the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Bowcaster\" title=\"Bowcaster\">Bowcaster</a>. However, its use of a magnetic field generator makes the weapon substantially quieter than other Ranged Weapons, making it ideal for game hunters who track prey easily spooked by the sudden bursts of light and loud noises of blasters. </p><p>Its lack of noise gives a Magna Caster a +5 <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Equipment\" title=\"Equipment\">Equipment</a> bonus to <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Stealth\" title=\"Stealth\">Stealth</a> checks made to <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Snipe\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Snipe\">Snipe</a>. A Magna Caster uses a case of bolts instead of a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Power_Pack\" title=\"Power Pack\">Power Pack</a>. After 10 shots, the case must be replaced. A case of 10 bolts costs 50 credits and weighs 1 kg. </p><p><b>Accurate:</b> This weapon takes no penalty when firing at targets at Short&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Range\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Range\">Range</a>. </p>",
